  simply help  far too few people and give the federal  government an  out in offering adequate compensation  to the descendants of slavery we know  america can do it on the federal level  we just saw about 10 trillion dollars be  printed for covet relief it didn't  affect any budgets  there's no inflation they just printed  the money  so we want to see that on a federal  level for  every american descendant of slavery not  just those  in one particular municipality the  compensation may be imperfect  and long overdue but it started a  national conversation  about how to repair racism every great  journey starts with the first step  i think people should embrace it yes  there's going to be flaws like anything  else  but if we never get started then what a  small step  but is in the right direction sally  lockwood sky news  evanston illinois
 

